# Code owners review the pull requests that change what the project publishes: the release
# builds, their signatures and notes, what the packages hold and the licenses shipped in them,
# the models the app offers for download, and the public pages. The branch rulesets require a
# code owner's approval for these files. Other files have no owner, and the pull-request skill
# (skills/pull-request/SKILL.md, "CIとマージの条件") says who may merge them.
#
# A pull request opened from a code owner's own account cannot be approved by that account, so
# only a code owner merges it, past the ruleset. Keep the skill in step when this list changes.
#
# Each entry is a plain path from the repository root, a folder ending in "/", with no wildcards:
# the skill matches a branch's files against these paths as they are written, and
# tests/devtools/test_codeowners.py checks that each one exists.
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

